Every claimed Wave 2 feature clears its transparent registration floor in the default bottle model. The narrowest margins are Hexyl Acetate 10% and Allyl Cyclohexyl Propionate 10%, which still clear the screen.

## Habanolide restoration

Your existing bottle ledger says the original 2% Habanolide row was omitted. Therefore the recommended final operation is:

```text
Habanolide neat: 118.577 µL
```

That gives approximately **3,722 ppm product basis** in the final default bottle and a **12.4×** registration ratio.

**Skip this line only if you have already added the full Habanolide correction.**

## Resulting concentration

### Wave 2 without Habanolide restoration

```text
Current physical bottle: 30.54 mL
+ Wave 2 module:        1.2 mL
= Final volume:         31.74 mL

Concentrate:            7.74 mL
Final concentration:    24.39% v/v
```

### Recommended, including the omitted Habanolide line

```text
Final volume:         31.859 mL
Concentrate:          7.859 mL
Final concentration:  24.67% v/v
```

No ethanol top-up is required because you explicitly prefer the higher concentration.

## OAV gate

Strict OAV is **WITHHELD**, not failed. A valid OAV requires a concentration and an odor threshold measured in a context-compatible matrix, route and method. Those data are unavailable for most of these proprietary materials and naturals in a hydroalcoholic fine-fragrance matrix.

The formula therefore uses two separate checks:

1. **Registration gate:** active-equivalent finished ppm divided by a conservative, transparent potency-class floor.
2. **Headspace gate:** a relative three-window model testing whether the intended block gains visibility without replacing the iris identity.

The registration floors are not odor thresholds and must not be renamed OAVs.

